  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Patnana Suresh Kumar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh, on 5 August, 2021 The Hon'Ble Smt Justice Lalitha Kanneganti Criminal Petition No.4417 Of 2021 Order:",
    "facts": "- This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 seeking a direction to the Station House Officer, Palakonda Police Station, Srikakulam District concerned to release all the tobacco products seized in connection with Crime No.177 of 2018. 2. The above said crime has been registered against the petitioners under Sections 188, 270, 272, 273, 328 r/w 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 and under Sections 57(1), 58, 59 r/w 30(1) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 on the allegation of illegal possession and transportation of prohibited and noxious food material branding as Gutka, Khaini and Pan Masala of 13 bags worth of Rs.1,85,700/-. Subsequent to registration of the crime, the petitioners approached this Court by way of filing Criminal Petition No.2332 of 2021 with a prayer to quash the F.I.R. and the same was allowed vide order dated 15-04-2021, as such the petitioners are entitled for return of tobacco products.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that Section 451 Cr.P.C. applies for return of the property pending investigation, Section 452 applies to a case where trial is concluded and Section 457 of Cr.P.C. applies where the property is not produced during trial.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that Section 451 Cr.P.C. applies for return of the property pending investigation, Section 452 applies to a case where trial is concluded and Section 457 of Cr.P.C. applies where the property is not produced during trial.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
